            The sequence at the bottom is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twistor+fibration"} twistor fibration
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#EquivariantStructure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(3)
            \- and
            = succeed "-Equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 5
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(5)
          %p
            Since the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associative+algebra"} algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+orthogonal+group"} special orthogonal group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(3)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Aut
                    %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℍ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{R}}(\mathbb{H}) \simeq SO(3)
          %p
            acting by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rotation"} rotation
            of the imaginary quaternions, via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+construction"} Hopf construction
            it follows that the 7-sphere and 4-sphere inherit
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(3)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/actions"} actions
            under which the quaternionic Hopf map is equivariant.
          %p
            Notice that this means that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(3)
            acts on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^7
            here diagonally on the
            %em two
            copies of the imaginary octonions in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 7
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ℍ
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi ℍ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^7 \hookrightarrow \mathbb{H} \oplus \mathbb{H}
            (as opposed to, say, via any one of the embeddings
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(3) \hookrightarrow SO(8)
            and the following canonical action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 8
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(8)
            on
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 7
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 8
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^7 \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}^8
          %p
            (see also
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#CookCrabb93"} Cook-Crabb 93
          %p But in fact more is true:
          #Spin5EquivarianceOfQuaternionicHopfFibration.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%285%29"}> Spin(5)
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} equivariance
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+Hopf+fibration"} quaternionic Hopf fibration
            %p Consider
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin%285%29"} Spin(5)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
                  on the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-sphere"} 4-sphere
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
