                  }
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#HasudaTomizawa09"}> Hasuda-Tomizawa 09, table 1
            )
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Of the resulting
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sp%282%29"} Sp(2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \times
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sp%281%29"} Sp(1)
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/7-sphere"} 7-sphere
              (from Prop.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#Spin5EquivarianceOfQuaternionicHopfFibration"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+group"} quotient group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sp%282%29.Sp%281%29"} Sp(2).Sp(1)
              acts
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+action"} effectively
          %h3#ClassInTheHomotopyGroupsOfSpheres Class in the homotopy groups of spheres
          %p
            The quaternionic Hopf fibration gives an element in the 7th
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} homotopy group of the 4-sphere
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi ℍ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 7
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 12
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [p_{\mathbb{H}}] \in \pi_7(S^4) \simeq \mathbb{Z} \times (\mathbb{Z}/12)
          %p and in fact it is a generator of the non-torsion factor in this group.
          %p
            Stably, i.e. as a generator for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} stable homotopy groups of spheres
            in degree
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 7
                    %mo −
                    %mn 4
                    %mo =
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 7-4 = 3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroup"} torsion
            generator:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi p
                    %mi ℍ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∈
                  %msubsup
                    %mi π
                    %mn 3
                    %mi S
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 24
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [p_{\mathbb{H}}] \in \pi_3^S \simeq \mathbb{Z}/24
                  \\,,.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/third+stable+homotopy+group+of+spheres"} third stable homotopy group of spheres
            (the third
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+stem"} stable stem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic group
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/order+of+a+group"} order
            24:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi π
                            %mn 3
                            %mi s
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 24
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msub
                            %mi h
                            %mi ℍ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↔
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\pi_3^s &amp;\simeq&amp; \mathbb{Z}/24
                  \\\
                  [h_{\mathbb{H}}] &amp;\leftrightarrow&amp; [1]
                  }
          %p
            where the generator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 24
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [1] \in \mathbb{Z}/24
            is represented by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+Hopf+fibration"} quaternionic Hopf fibration
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 7
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mi ℍ
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^7 \overset{h_{\mathbb{H}}}{\longrightarrow} S^4
          %p
            Under the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin-Thom+isomorphism"} Pontrjagin-Thom isomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} stable homotopy groups of spheres
            with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bordism+ring"} bordism ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                    %mi fr
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^{fr}_\bullet
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+framing"} stably framed
            manifolds (see at
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MFr"} MFr
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-sphere"} 3-sphere
            (with its left-invariant framing induced from the identification with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SU%282%29"} SU(2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≃
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sp%281%29"} Sp(1)
            )
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi π
                            %mn 3
                            %mi s
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mn 3
                            %mi fr
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msub
                            %mi h
                            %mi ℍ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↔
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 3
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\pi_3^s &amp; \simeq &amp; \Omega_3^{fr}
                  \\\
                  [h_{\mathbb{H}}] &amp; \leftrightarrow &amp; [S^3]
                  \\,.
                  }
          %p
            Moreover, the relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                  %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2 4 [S^3] \,\simeq\, 0
            is represented by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bordism"} bordism
            which is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complement"} complement
            of 24
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+balls"} open balls
            inside
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+the"} the
            = succeed "-manifold" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K3"} K3
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "third+stable+homotopy+group+of+spheres#WangXu10"} Wang-Xu 10, Sec. 2.6
          %h3#ClassInEquivariantStableHomotopyTheory Class in equivariant stable homotopy theory
          %p
            Fix a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \hookrightarrow SO(3)
            which does not come from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(2) \hookrightarrow SO(3)
            – i.e. not a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group"} cyclic group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dihedral+groups"} dihedral groups
            or else the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tetrahedral+group"} tetrahedral group
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octahedral+group"} octahedral group
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/icosahedral+group"} icosahedral group
            (by the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+classification"} ADE classification
          %p
            Regard both
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^7
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^4
            as pointed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+G-spaces"} topological G-spaces
            via the
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(3)
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#EquivariantStructure"} above
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi G
                    %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 7
                  %mo ,
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi G
                    %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi G
                  %mi Spectra
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Sigma^\infty_G S^7, \Sigma^\infty_G S^4 \in G Spectra
          %p
            for the corresponding
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+suspension+spectra"} equivariant suspension spectra
          %p
            Notice that if we took trivial
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+category"} stable homotopy category
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 7
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mn 24
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\Sigma^\infty S^7, \Sigma^\infty S^4] \simeq \mathbb{Z}/24
          %p
            by the
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ClassInTheHomotopyGroupsOfSpheres"} above
            %sup#fnref:1
              %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
          #QuaternionicHopfFibrationIsDEEquivariantlyStablyNonTorsion.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              In
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+theory"} equivariant homotopy theory
              this becomes a non-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/torsion+subgroup"}> torsion group
              , i.e.
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi G
                      %mn ∞
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 7
                    %mo ,
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi G
                      %mn ∞
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 4
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi G
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi ⋯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [\Sigma^\infty_G S^7, \Sigma^\infty_G S^4]_G \simeq \mathbb{Z} \oplus \cdots
            %p
              with the quaternionic Hopf fibration, regarded as a
              = succeed "-equivariant" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              First use the
              %a{:href => "rational+equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory#SplittingIntoMackeyFunctors"} Greenlees-May decomposition
              which says that for any two
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+spectra"} equivariant spectra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X,Y
              and writing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_\bullet(X), \pi_\bullet(Y)
              for their
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+groups"} equivariant homotopy groups
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mackey+functors"} Mackey functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo ↦
                    %msubsup
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \mapsto \pi_n^H(X)
              for all subgroups
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                      %mo ⊂
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H \subset G
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi G
                    %mo ⟶
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [X,Y]_G
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\underset{n}{\oplus}
                    Hom_{\mathcal{M}[G]}(\pi_n(X), \pi_n(Y))
            %p
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} rationally
              an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %p
              With this we are reduced to showing that there exists
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{Z}
              and a morphism of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mackey+functors"} Mackey functors
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+groups"} equivariant homotopy groups
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi G
                      %mn ∞
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 7
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi G
                      %mn ∞
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(\Sigma^\infty_G S^7) \to \pi_n(\Sigma^\infty_G S^4)
              which is not a torsion element in the abelian
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-group
              of Mackey functors.
            %p
              To analyse this, we use the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tom+Dieck+splitting"} tom Dieck splitting
              which says that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+homotopy+groups"} equivariant homotopy groups
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+suspension+spectra"} equivariant suspension spectra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi G
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^\infty_G X
              contain a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct summand
              which is simply the ordinary stable homotopy groups of the naive
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point"} fixed point
              space
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi X
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^H
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi G
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_n^H(\Sigma^\infty_G X) \simeq \pi_n(\Sigma^\infty (X^H)) \oplus \cdots
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now observe that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+points"} fixed points
              of the
              = succeed "-action" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi SO
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(3)
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+Hopf+fibration"} real Hopf fibration
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi ℍ
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi SO
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 3
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi ℝ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (p_{\mathbb{H}})^{SO(3)} = p_{\mathbb{R}} \;\colon\; S^1 \longrightarrow S^1
            %p
              since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(3)
              acts transitively on the quaternionic quaternions and fixes the real quaternions. By our assumption that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \subset SO(3)
              does not come through
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi SO
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 3
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(2) \hookrightarrow SO(3)
              it follows that this statment is still true for
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi ℍ
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi G
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi p
                      %mi ℝ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (p_{\mathbb{H}})^{G} = p_{\mathbb{R}} \;\colon\; S^1 \longrightarrow S^1
                    \\,.
            %p
              But the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+Hopf+fibration"} real Hopf fibration
              defines a non-torsion element in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                        %mi S
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0^S \simeq \mathbb{Z}
            %p
              In conclusion then, at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo =
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H = G
              we find that the
              = succeed "-equivariant" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                      %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi G
                      %mn ∞
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 7
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msubsup
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                      %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi G
                      %mn ∞
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{Ab}(\pi_1^G(\Sigma^\infty_G S^7), \pi_1^G(\Sigma^\infty_G S^4))
            %p which appears as a non-torsion element in
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℳ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi G
                      %mn ∞
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 7
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi G
                      %mn ∞
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom_{\mathcal{M}[G]}( \pi_1(\Sigma^\infty_G S^7), \pi_1(\Sigma^\infty_G S^4) )
            %p
              and hence in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi G
                        %mn ∞
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 7
                      %mo ,
                      %msubsup
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi G
                        %mn ∞
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 4
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma^\infty_G S^7, \Sigma^\infty_G S^4]_G
          %p
            See also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+cohomotopy"} equivariant stable cohomotopy
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+Hopf+fibration"}> real Hopf fibration
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+Hopf+fibration"} complex Hopf fibration
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonionic+Hopf+fibration"} octonionic Hopf fibration
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Calabi-Penrose+fibration"} Calabi-Penrose fibration
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+projective+space"} quaternionic projective space
          %h2#references References
          %p The original article:
          %ul
            %li#Hopf35
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heinz+Hopf"}> Heinz Hopf
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Über die Abbildungen von Sphären auf Sphäre niedrigerer Dimension
              %strong 25
              1 (1935) 427-440 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://eudml.org/doc/212801"}> eudml:212801
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Further discussion:
          %ul
            %li#GluckWarnerZiller86
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Herman+Gluck"}> Herman Gluck
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Warner"} Frank Warner
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfgang+Ziller"} Wolfgang Ziller
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The geometry of the Hopf fibrations
                %strong 32
                (1986), 173-198 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/266548925_The_geometry_of_the_Hopf_fibrations"}> ResearchGate
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GluckWarnerZiller-HopfFibrations.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Miyaoka93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reiko+Miyaoka"}> Reiko Miyaoka
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    The linear isotropy group of
                    = succeed "," do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi G
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi SO
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 4
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_2/SO(4)
                %strong 30
                2 (1993) 179-202 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.ojm/1200784357"}> Euclid
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Porteous95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ian+Porteous"}> Ian Porteous
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Clifford Algebras and the Classical Groups
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511470912"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511470912
            %li#HasudaTomizawa09
              %p
                Machiko Hatsuda, Shinya Tomizawa,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Coset for Hopf fibration and Squashing
                %strong 26
                225007 (2009) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0906.1025"}> arXiv:0906.1025
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/0264-9381/26/22/225007"} doi:10.1088/0264-9381/26/22/225007
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rustam+Sadykov"}> Rustam Sadykov
                , §8.3 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Elements of Surgery Theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.math.ksu.edu/~sadykov/Lecture%20Notes/Surgery%20Theory.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/SadykovSurgeryTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tyrone+Cutler"}> Tyrone Cutler
                , p. 23 of:
                %em Fibrations IV
                (2020) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.uni-bielefeld.de/~tcutler/pdf/Fibrations%20IV.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Cutler-FibrationsIV.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+homotopy+theory"} parameterized homotopy theory
            includes
          %ul
            %li#CookCrabb93
              %p
                A. L. Cook, M. C. Crabb,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Fiberwise Hopf structures on sphere bundles
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~aar/papers/crabbcook.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Iriye95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kouyemon+Iriye"}> Kouyemon Iriye
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Equivariant Hopf structures on a sphere
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.kjm/1250518704"} Euclid
          %p
            Discussion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrik+Buchholtz"}> Ulrik Buchholtz
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Egbert+Rijke"} Egbert Rijke
              %em The Cayley-Dickson Construction in Homotopy Type Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.01134"}> arXiv:1610.01134
              )
          %p
            Noteworthy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+products"} fiber products
            with the quaternionic Hopf fibration, notably
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exotic+7-spheres"} exotic 7-spheres
          %ul
            %li
              Llohann D. Sperança,
              %em Explicit Constructions over the Exotic 8-sphere
              (
              %a{:href => "https://www.ime.unicamp.br/~rigas/sigma8EncontroTopol.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/SperancaExoticSpheres.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          .footnotes
            %hr/
            %ol
              %li#fn:1
                %p
                  The proof of prop.
                  %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuaternionicHopfFibrationIsDEEquivariantlyStablyNonTorsion"}
                  profited from
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"} Charles Rezk
                  %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/a/224185/381"} here
                  that the reduction to fixed points will make the real Hopf fibration give a non-torsion contribution, and from
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Barnes"} David Barnes
                  who amplified the use of the Greenless-May splitting theorem.
                  %a{:href => "#fnref:1", :rev => "footnote"} ↩
